From 4d042d88fe6b805d6106707b7dff4d6b65e322ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:21:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] drm/apple: Refuse panel brightness once the display
 processor crashed

A panel that presents its level in the swap gets a new level only with
a present. Once the IOMFB queue has timed out and marked the processor
crashed, every present is discarded, but brightness writes were still
accepted and actual_brightness kept reporting the last requested level,
so userspace saw a level change that never reached the panel.

Fail both with -EIO while the processor is crashed.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 39ca9e2968ea9bdd8edd0397e1f61a32b3b45044)
(cherry picked from commit e25c83799018ef5c61525efe230a827f442930c1)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
index 00f29157241f..46c162f20121 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
@@ -246,6 +246,9 @@ static int dcp_get_brightness(struct backlight_device *bd)
 
 	if (READ_ONCE(dcp->quiescing))
 		return -ENODEV;
+	/* Nothing is presented any more: there is no level to report. */
+	if (READ_ONCE(dcp->crashed))
+		return -EIO;
 
 	if (dcp_backlight_active(dcp) || dcp_backlight_desktop(dcp)) {
 		/*
@@ -772,6 +775,9 @@ static int dcp_set_brightness(struct backlight_device *bd)
 
 	if (READ_ONCE(dcp->quiescing))
 		return -ENODEV;
+	/* A crashed processor discards every present, the level with it. */
+	if (READ_ONCE(dcp->crashed))
+		return -EIO;
 
 	if (dcp_backlight_active(dcp) || dcp_backlight_desktop(dcp)) {
 		struct dcp_backlight_state *state = &dcp->backlight.state;
-- 
