From 9201da58be4e7dddd085314552e017621addcfce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] drm/asahi: t6050: identify the 27.2 (26B8125) G17S
 firmware of the K114/K116

Applies on top of aurora-silicon/linux PR #1173.

The 16-inch M5 Pro OLED (K116s, Mac17,12) restores from
UniversalMac_27.2_26B8125_Restore.ipsw, not from the 26B123 image of the
Mac17,8 that #1173 pins. Its Firmware/agx/armfw_g17x.im4p and
armfw1_g17x.im4p carry a010 (G17S) images whose LC_UUIDs are the uuid of
the K116s ADT's iop-gfx-nub and iop-gfx1-nub (8A2891FC-D479-37E8-895D-
71B4D88ECB51, 58FF964E-F74B-31C2-8179-3837D6ADA9C2), so this is what iBoot
loads. TEXT 0x50000 + 0x54000, DATA 0x184000, the GKTS/ECAP records and
the _rtk_tunables/_rtk_patchbay sections at 26B123's offsets, but the
fwid digest differs:

  26B8125 G17S  af68d034a3f006b43dab661b825f12598cb86e4d2a0e3844f14fa5059f38f6cb
  26B123  G17S  2b4613c62a8a007f22a94101702c9ac6c4e90f2e123f3b36fbe6ffea913f0fd9

(check_fwid.py's algorithm.) Without this
entry the driver refuses the K116s firmware before any GPU write.

It names V26B123_M5: the AGX kext of the 26B8125 kernelcache builds root
version word 0x0c8e_4339_8728_04c0 and its u64[24] allocation size table
is ABI_ALLOCATION_SIZES_26B123_M5 entry for entry (HW data 0x2850, policy
0x12728, status config 0x790), and both firmware roles build the same
version word. The interior
offsets of the policy and the status config were not compared against
26B123's and no 27.2 firmware has run this graph on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
